topic_17_nighthaven_body_07_18:
According to the framework program (liturgical, cultural and scientifical),

I. In the first semester of this year, the theme “Solemn Year of the Banning of Fishing” will be approached as follows:

Methods of Fish-related care and assistance of the Fishing-sick described in the Holy Scriptures;
The Fish-work of the Church and its servants for the care of the Fishing-sick;
The social-philanthropic and ultimately medical endeavours of the Royal Church of Durevos.

topic_17_nighthaven_body_07_19:
II. In the second semester of this year, “Commemorative Year of All Things Not Fishing” will be approached as follows:

The King of Durevos, the Physician of our souls and bodies;
The unmercenary saints and the significance of their veneration;
Holy healers in the history of the Church.

Following discussions in plenary session, at the proposal of the Fishing Guilds, Monastic and Social Committees, the Crowned King of Durevos, the Dragon resolved:

topic_17_nighthaven_body_07_20:
To approve the declaration of this year as “Solemn Year of the Banning of Fishing” and “Commemorative Year of All Things Not Fishing” in the Nighthaven Patriarchate;

To approve the framework program (including theological-educational, cultural and surreptitious activities) entitled “This Year – Solemn Year of the Banning of Fishing and Commemorative Year of All Things Not Fishing.”

Chairman of the Royal Church

topic_17_nighthaven_body_16_01:
I know the number of the sands and the measure of the seas;
With sinking steps, a path over moonlit dunes winds but never stops,
An imperfect lioness rides a celestial chariot on a road of midday stars;
Golden is the carriage and golden are the wheels.

